    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "2020218058845847564",
      "url": "https://x.com/CataPaul2/status/2020218058845847564",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/CataPaul2/status/2020218058845847564",
      "text": "🍔  Cities with highest consumption of burgers\n\n1.🇺🇸 Las Vegas, USA\nHighest global density with 21.5 burger shops per capita.\n\n2.🇺🇸 New York City, USA\nMassive volume driven by high-traffic global burger icons.\n\n3.🇺🇸 Chicago, USA\nDeeply rooted fast-food culture and iconic gourmet styles.\n\n4.🇬🇧 London, UK\nEurope’s leading hub for premium craft burger innovation.\n\n5.🇺🇸 Houston, USA\nHuge per-capita intake with dominant regional chains.\n\n6.🇺🇸 Los Angeles, USA\nHigh market volume and birthplace of smash burgers.\n\n7.🇦🇺 Sydney, Australia\nBooming craft scene fueled by high meat consumption.\n\n8.🇫🇷 Paris, France\nMassive McDonald’s market, outpacing traditional French bakery items.\n\n9.🇺🇸 Richmond, USA\nStatistically holds the highest restaurant-to-resident burger ratio.\n\n10.🇯🇵 Tokyo, Japan\nRapid growth mixing Western brands and local fusion.\n\n11.🇪🇸 Barcelona, Spain\nHome to the world’s current top-ranked burger restaurant.\n\n12.🇦🇷 Buenos Aires, Argentina\nTraditional high beef intake meeting modern burger trends.\n\n13.🇵🇭 Manila, Philippines\nHigh demand for American styles and local favorites.\n\n14.🇩🇪 Berlin, Germany\nDense concentration of shops with strong historical ties.\n\n15.🇰🇷 Seoul, South Korea\nGen Z driving demand for “Instagrammable” premium burgers.",
